\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Filament width vs Mach number from MHD simulations ($\beta = 1$). Blue circles show measured widths, red dashed line shows sonic scale theory ($\lambda \propto {\cal  M}^{-2}$), and green dotted line shows the observed value ($0.1$\nobreakspace  {}pc). The simulations confirm the theoretical prediction across an order of magnitude in Mach number.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mhd_mach}{{2}{4}{Filament width vs Mach number from MHD simulations ($\beta = 1$). Blue circles show measured widths, red dashed line shows sonic scale theory ($\lambda \propto {\cal M}^{-2}$), and green dotted line shows the observed value ($0.1$~pc). The simulations confirm the theoretical prediction across an order of magnitude in Mach number}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Filament width vs plasma beta from MHD simulations (${\cal  M} = 5$). The width shows minimal dependence on $\beta $, consistent with the sonic scale theory. The observed value of $0.1$\nobreakspace  {}pc is shown as a red dashed line.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mhd_beta}{{3}{4}{Filament width vs plasma beta from MHD simulations (${\cal M} = 5$). The width shows minimal dependence on $\beta $, consistent with the sonic scale theory. The observed value of $0.1$~pc is shown as a red dashed line}{figure.3}{}}
